# Settings of the local W-Stack. Copy to settings.env (ignored by git) or to a
# file outside the repository and point WSTACK_SETTINGS at it; the scripts
# source it. A value set in the environment wins over the file.

# A wildcard DNS zone whose names all resolve to the W-Stack node's address.
# The tenant's host is <TENANT>.<WSTACK_ZONE>, and wallets, the guard and the
# W-Stack's own services reach it by that name. Empty: up.sh creates the
# cluster, then uses <node address>.sslip.io (a wildcard DNS service, no setup)
# and keeps it with the address in $WSTACK_STATE_DIR/zone.env.
WSTACK_ZONE=${WSTACK_ZONE:-}

# The node's address that zone is built on. When set, every script refuses to
# run if the node holds another one (after a reboot, Docker may hand addresses
# out in another order). Recorded in zone.env when up.sh picks the zone.
WSTACK_NODE_IP=${WSTACK_NODE_IP:-}

# The kind cluster and its Docker network. A network of its own keeps the
# node's address stable: docker network create wstack, then WSTACK_NETWORK=wstack.
WSTACK_CLUSTER=${WSTACK_CLUSTER:-wstack}            # context kind-wstack, node wstack-control-plane
WSTACK_NETWORK=${WSTACK_NETWORK:-kind}
WSTACK_HOST_PORTS=${WSTACK_HOST_PORTS:-0}              # 1: also publish the node's ports 80/443 on this machine

# The tenant (the tenant chart of eclipse-xfsc/deployment).
TENANT=${TENANT:-connector}
TENANT_NS=${TENANT_NS:-ocm-wstack}
TENANT_GROUP=${TENANT_GROUP:-default}
TENANT_KEY=${TENANT_KEY:-eckey}
GW_NODEPORT=${GW_NODEPORT:-32091}                # the tenant's HTTPS listener on the envoy gateway

# Where things are.
# DEPLOYMENT_DIR=../deployment   # clone of eclipse-xfsc/deployment (default: next to this repository)
# WSTACK_STATE_DIR=~/.local/state/facis-wstack-local/wstack   # local CA, patched chart copies
# WSTACK_LOCK=infrastructure/wstack/wstack-images.lock.tsv
# ALLOW_UNPINNED=1               # deploy another deployment commit than the lock's, knowingly
